  "name": "X-OmniClaw Technical Report: A Unified Mobile Agent for Multimodal Understanding and Interaction",
  "notes": "The report presents demonstrations. Its behavior-cloning component captures runtime skills; it does not establish policy-weight imitation training, and literal trace replay is described as future work. No general benchmark result or release completeness is inferred. Basis: complete retained abstract and source-reviewed sections of the exact-version paper (2 Framework; 3 Omni Perception; 4 Omni Memory; 5.1 Omni Action in App Ecosystem; 5.2 Trajectory Cloned Execution); not an entire-paper reading or reproduction claim.",
  "published_at": "2026-05-07",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "Describes an Android agent architecture combining multimodal perception, working and personal memory, hybrid XML/visual grounding, and reusable skills captured from user interactions.",
